<% @title = "For public authorities" %>

<%# The id "copyright" is linked to from core and must stay
    (bundle exec rake themes:check_help_sections). %>
<%= page_band %>
<%= render :partial => 'sidebar' %>

<div id="left_column_flip" class="left_column_flip">
  <dl>

    <dt id="top">I followed a link at the bottom of a request. What is this site? <a href="#top" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></dt>
    <dd>
      <p><%= site_name %> is a site for making Freedom of Information
        requests. The request you received was written here and sent to your
        authority by email. Handle it like any other request from a member of
        the public.</p>
      <p>This copy of the site is a demonstration: its authorities and
        requests are invented.</p>
    </dd>

    <dt id="reply">How do I reply? <a href="#reply" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></dt>
    <dd>
      <p>Reply to the email in the usual way. Each request is sent from its
        own address, and a reply to that address is filed with the request.
        Please don't send the reply to a different address.</p>
    </dd>

    <dt id="email_only">Is an email address enough for a valid request? <a href="#email_only" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></dt>
    <dd>
      <p>Yes. The Freedom of Information Act asks for the requester's name and
        "an address for correspondence", and an email address is one.</p>
    </dd>

    <dt id="responses">Will our reply be published? <a href="#responses" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></dt>
    <dd>
      <p>The request and its correspondence stay private. A document from your
        reply may be published separately, after an administrator has checked
        it and its details.</p>
    </dd>

    <dt id="names">Are the names of our staff published? <a href="#names" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></dt>
    <dd>
      <p>Only if they appear in a document that's published after checking.
        The requester can also redact names before a document is published.
        If something has been published that shouldn't have been, use the
        <a href="<%= help_contact_path %>">contact page</a>.</p>
    </dd>

    <dt id="days">How is the deadline on a request page worked out? <a href="#days" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></dt>
    <dd>
      <p>A request is shown as overdue
        <%= AlaveteliConfiguration.reply_late_after_days %> working days after
        it was sent, not counting weekends and public holidays, and as long
        overdue after <%= AlaveteliConfiguration.reply_very_late_after_days %>.
        If you ask the requester to clarify the request, the count starts
        again from the clarification. If you extend the deadline, as the law
        allows, the requester can record the new date.</p>
    </dd>

    <dt id="allowed_responses">Our reply to an old request was returned <a href="#allowed_responses" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></dt>
    <dd>
      <p>A request that has had no activity for some months stops accepting
        replies, to keep out spam. Use the
        <a href="<%= help_contact_path %>">contact page</a> and the reply can
        be added by hand.</p>
    </dd>

    <dt id="copyright"><a id="commercial"></a>What about copyright in the documents we send? <a href="#copyright" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a></dt>
    <dd>
      <p>Copyright in a reply stays with the authority or whoever else owns
        it. If you believe that publishing a particular document infringes
        copyright, use the <a href="<%= help_contact_path %>">contact page</a>
        and say which one.</p>
    </dd>

  </dl>

  <div id="hash_link_padding"></div>
</div>
